{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI write from Paris, exhausted but delighted. Yesterday I walked at Saint-Cloud, watching the Seine flow by; the water was calm, reflecting the autumn light in a way that reminded me of the quiet dignity of the Rhine. But tonight was peculiar. I attended a three-act ballet concerning a sleepwalker found in a nobleman’s bedroom, later seen crossing a roof with a lantern. It was strange: only the first act was danced; the rest was merely mimed. One sees the tension between movement and stillness, the body acting without the full presence of the soul. It is a strange spectacle, yet it captures something of the unconscious mind’s wanderings.\n\nI am safe and well, though the French air is thick. I think of you and the boys in Berlin. The journey continues, but my heart remains with you.\n\nYour loving,\nWilhelm"}}],"created":1795080555,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":186,"prompt_tokens":932,"total_tokens":1118,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-fkW85dAlMUdpSLuZ5J483wXn6e83LMuj","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":932,"prompt_ms":920.669,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9878422746781116,"prompt_per_second":1012.3073547605056,"predicted_n":186,"predicted_ms":4412.12,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.849297297297298,"predicted_per_second":41.929956574163896}}